---
import run from '../../public/assets/benchmarks/hindsight-jev/live-results.json';
const labels: Record<string,string> = {baseline:'Worker only',memory:'Hindsight',jev:'Jev',combined:'Hindsight + Jev'};
const modes = ['baseline','memory','jev','combined'] as const;
---
<figure class="memory-live" aria-label="Live four-configuration benchmark results">
  <div class="memory-live__heading"><span class="memory-eyebrow">Live services · exploratory benchmark</span><strong>{run.trials.length} requests · 8 cases · 2 repeats</strong></div>
  <div class="memory-live__rows">
    {modes.map(mode=>{const s=run.summary[mode]; return <div class="memory-live__row">
      <strong>{labels[mode]}</strong>
      <div class="memory-live__track" aria-hidden="true"><span style={`width:${100*s.correct/s.n}%`}></span></div>
      <span><b>{s.correct}/{s.n}</b> successful</span>
      <span><b>{s.median_total_seconds.toFixed(2)} s</b> median</span>
    </div>;})}
  </div>
  <div class="article-table memory-decision-table" role="region" aria-label="Live benchmark error and withholding counts" tabindex="0">
    <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Configuration</th><th scope="col">Accepted non-success</th><th scope="col">Withheld</th><th scope="col">Service errors</th></tr></thead><tbody>{modes.map(mode=><tr><th scope="row">{labels[mode]}</th><td>{run.summary[mode].accepted_wrong}</td><td>{run.summary[mode].withheld}</td><td>{run.summary[mode].errors}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Same Muse Glimmer worker and strict JSON scoring. Unknown/scope cases allow correct clarification. Withholding a known answer does not count as success. Accepted non-success includes unknown answers on known-fact questions. All errors remain in the denominator; repeated cases are not independent tasks.</figcaption>
  <p><a href="/assets/benchmarks/hindsight-jev/live-results.json">Raw inputs and responses</a> · <a href="/assets/benchmarks/hindsight-jev/LIVE-REPORT.md">Recomputed report</a> · <a href="/assets/benchmarks/hindsight-jev/LIVE-PROTOCOL.md">Protocol and scoring</a></p>
</figure>
<style>
.memory-live {width:min(100%,var(--reading-width)); margin:2rem auto;}
.memory-live .article-table {overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%;}
.memory-live__heading {display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:.5rem;padding:1rem 0;border-top:2px solid var(--blue);}
.memory-live__heading strong {font-size:.85rem;}
.memory-live__rows {display:grid;gap:1rem;padding:1rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);}
.memory-live__row {display:grid;grid-template-columns:9rem minmax(2rem,1fr) 7.5rem 7rem;align-items:center;gap:1rem;font-size:.85rem;}
.memory-live__track {height:.65rem;background:var(--accent-soft);}
.memory-live__track span {display:block;height:100%;background:var(--blue);}
.memory-live__row b {font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}
figcaption,p {text-align:left;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.7;color:var(--post-muted);}
@media(max-width:640px){.memory-live__row{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.45rem}.memory-live__track{grid-column:1/-1;grid-row:2}.memory-live__row>strong{grid-column:1/-1}}
</style>
